class.description:
A dummy [TextSystem] interface that doesn't do anything. Useful for freeing up memory when rendering text is not needed, as text servers are resource-intensive. It can also be used for performance comparisons in complex GUIs to check the impact of text rendering.
A dummy text server is always available at the start of a project. Here's how to access it:
[codeblock]
var dummy_text_system = TextSystemManager.find_interface("Dummy")
if dummy_text_system != null:
	TextSystemManager.set_primary_interface(dummy_text_system)
	# If the other text servers are unneeded, they can be removed:
	for i in TextSystemManager.get_interface_count():
		var text_system = TextSystemManager.get_interface(i)
		if text_system != dummy_text_system:
			TextSystemManager.remove_interface(text_system)
[/codeblock]
The command line argument [code]--text-driver Dummy[/code] (case-sensitive) can be used to force the "Dummy" [TextSystem] on any project.
